# Writes and Actions with status, content type and deadline rejection

## Goal

Write a Property and invoke an Action on an HTTP Thing through the runtime,
with a bearer credential resolved just in time from a reference, and watch
the runtime refuse a wrong credential, a wrong response content type and an
exhausted deadline with distinct classes. The runtime's retry decision for a
permanent failure is `:stop`; nothing retries a rejected write.

## Prerequisites

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:wotex_lab, "~> 0.1.0"},
  {:req, "~> 0.7.4"},
  {:bandit, "~> 1.12"},
  {:plug, "~> 1.18"}
])
```

The requirements above are published-artifact requirements. At the time this
notebook was written none of the `wotex*` packages is published on Hex; the
notebook is verified against the workspace source cohort recorded in
`priv/provenance/source-cohort.json` by `test/wotex/lab/cookbook_test.exs`,
which evaluates every Elixir cell below in order (skipping this install
cell). `Mix.install/1` never points at a Git checkout.

## Package and consumer ownership

| Concern | Owner | Where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Operation and Form selection, input carriage, status mapping, retry classes | `wotex_runtime`, `wotex_binding_http` (package-implements) | `ConsumedThing`, `Wotex.Binding.HTTP`, `Wotex.Runtime.Retry` |
| Credential references and just-in-time lookup | `wotex_lab` (consumer-implements `Wotex.Runtime.Credentials`) | `Wotex.Lab.Adapters.Runtime.StaticRef` |
| Bytes on the wire | `wotex_lab` (consumer-implements `Wotex.Binding.HTTP.Client`) | `ReqClient` |
| The server, its token check and its misbehaving action | this notebook | per-run `http_handler` function plug |

## Run

```elixir
alias Wotex.Binding.HTTP
alias Wotex.Lab.Adapters.HTTP.ReqClient
alias Wotex.Lab.Adapters.Runtime.StaticRef
alias Wotex.Lab.Telemetry
alias Wotex.Runtime.{ConsumedThing, Context, Error, Result, Retry}
alias Wotex.ThingDescription

telemetry_id = "cookbook-write-and-act-#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}"

events =
  for component <- Telemetry.components(),
      operation <- Telemetry.operations(),
      event <- [:start, :stop, :exception],
      do: [:wotex, :lab, component, operation, event]

:ok = :telemetry.attach_many(telemetry_id, events, &Telemetry.forward/4, self())
token = "room-token-7f3a"
```

The server checks the bearer token on writes, accepts the Action with `202`
and answers the `reboot` Action with HTML on purpose. Written values land in
an Agent so the effect is observable from outside the request. Both the handler
function and its store belong to this run; no shared module is recompiled.

```elixir
{:ok, store} = Agent.start_link(fn -> %{} end)

import Plug.Conn

http_handler = fn conn, store ->
  case {conn.method, conn.request_path} do
    {"PUT", "/properties/target"} ->
      case get_req_header(conn, "authorization") do
        ["Bearer " <> ^token] ->
          {:ok, body, conn} = read_body(conn)
          Agent.update(store, &Map.put(&1, :target, body))
          send_resp(conn, 204, "")

        _other ->
          send_resp(conn, 401, "")
      end

    {"POST", "/actions/set-target"} ->
      {:ok, body, conn} = read_body(conn)
      body = ~s({"status":"pending","input":#{body}})
      conn |> put_resp_content_type("application/json") |> send_resp(202, body)

    {"POST", "/actions/reboot"} ->
      conn |> put_resp_content_type("text/html") |> send_resp(200, "<b>rebooting</b>")

    {"GET", "/properties/slow"} ->
      Process.sleep(400)
      conn |> put_resp_content_type("application/json") |> send_resp(200, "1")

    _other ->
      send_resp(conn, 404, "")
  end
end

{:ok, server} =
  Bandit.start_link(
    plug: {http_handler, store},
    ip: {127, 0, 0, 1},
    port: 0,
    startup_log: false
  )

{:ok, {_ip, port}} = ThousandIsland.listener_info(server)
base = "http://127.0.0.1:#{port}/"
```

The fixture TD gains the `reboot` Action and the real base. Credentials are
references only: the secret is produced by the lookup function at request
time and never stored in the consumed Thing.

```elixir
fixture = Application.app_dir(:wotex_lab, "priv/fixtures/http/thing-description.json")
{:ok, fixture_td} = fixture |> File.read!() |> ThingDescription.parse()

reboot = %{
  "forms" => [%{"href" => "actions/reboot", "contentType" => "application/json", "op" => "invokeaction"}]
}

{:ok, td} =
  fixture_td
  |> ThingDescription.to_map()
  |> Map.put("base", base)
  |> put_in(["actions", "reboot"], reboot)
  |> ThingDescription.from_map()

{:ok, profile} = HTTP.profile()
{:ok, config} = HTTP.config(client: {ReqClient, %{receive_timeout: 2_000}})

credentials = fn secret ->
  {StaticRef,
   %{
     references: %{"bearer_sc" => "vault://room/http"},
     lookup: fn "vault://room/http" -> {:ok, {:bearer, secret}} end
   }}
end

consume = fn credential ->
  {:ok, consumed} =
    ConsumedThing.new(td,
      profiles: [profile],
      transports: %{profile.id => HTTP.transport(config)},
      credentials: credential
    )

  consumed
end

consumed = consume.(credentials.(token))
refute_token_in_state? = not (inspect(consumed) =~ token)
```

Write and invoke. A `204` becomes an `:ok` result with a `nil` payload; a
`202` becomes `:accepted` with the decoded body.

```elixir
context =
  Context.new!(request_id: "http-write", deadline: System.monotonic_time(:millisecond) + 2_000)

{:ok, %Result{} = write} =
  Telemetry.span(:runtime, :request, %{operation: :writeproperty, profile: :cookbook}, fn ->
    ConsumedThing.write_property(consumed, "target", 23.5, context)
  end)

{:ok, %Result{} = action} = ConsumedThing.invoke_action(consumed, "setTarget", 24, context)
stored = Agent.get(store, &Map.get(&1, :target))
{write.status, write.payload, action.status, action.payload, stored}
```

## Deliberate breakage

A wrong token is a permanent `401`; the error never echoes either token. The
HTML answer to `reboot` is a protocol error. A 100 ms deadline against a
400 ms server is a timeout. The runtime's retry policy stops on the
permanent failure.

```elixir
wrong = consume.(credentials.("wrong-token"))

{:error, %Error{class: denied_class} = denied} =
  ConsumedThing.write_property(wrong, "target", 1.0, context)

{:error, %Error{class: reboot_class} = reboot_error} =
  ConsumedThing.invoke_action(consumed, "reboot", nil, context)

quick = Context.new!(request_id: "http-late", deadline: System.monotonic_time(:millisecond) + 100)
{:error, %Error{class: late_class}} = ConsumedThing.read_property(consumed, "slow", quick)

decision = Retry.decision(:writeproperty, denied, attempt: 1, max_attempts: 3)
leak_free? = not (inspect(denied) =~ token) and not (inspect(denied) =~ "wrong-token")

%{
  denied: {denied_class, denied.details.cause.code, leak_free?},
  reboot: {reboot_class, reboot_error.details.cause.code},
  late: late_class,
  retry: decision,
  still_stored: Agent.get(store, &Map.get(&1, :target))
}
```

```elixir
:ok = ThousandIsland.stop(server)
:ok = Agent.stop(store)
```

## Safe telemetry

```elixir
drain = fn drain ->
  receive do
    {:wotex_lab_telemetry, event, measurements, metadata} ->
      [{event, measurements, metadata} | drain.(drain)]
  after
    0 -> []
  end
end

spans = drain.(drain)
:telemetry.detach(telemetry_id)
text = inspect(spans)
labels_safe? = not (text =~ token) and not (text =~ "wrong-token") and not (text =~ "23.5")
{length(spans), labels_safe?}
```

## Expected output

| Check | Expectation |
| --- | --- |
| `write-through-runtime` | The write is `:ok` with `nil` payload and the server stored `23.5` |
| `action-accepted` | `setTarget` is `:accepted` with the server's pending body |
| `unauthorized-permanent` | A wrong bearer is `:permanent` with cause `:http_status`; the stored value is unchanged |
| `no-credential-leak` | Neither token appears in the error, the consumed Thing or telemetry |
| `deadline-timeout` | A 100 ms deadline is class `:timeout` |
| `retry-decision-stop` | `Retry.decision/3` for the permanent failure is `:stop` |
| `media-type-refused` | The HTML action response is `:protocol` with cause `:unexpected_response_media_type` |

```elixir
%{
  "write-through-runtime" => write.status == :ok and write.payload == nil and stored == "23.5",
  "action-accepted" =>
    action.status == :accepted and action.payload == %{"status" => "pending", "input" => 24},
  "unauthorized-permanent" =>
    denied_class == :permanent and denied.details.cause.code == :http_status,
  "no-credential-leak" => leak_free? and refute_token_in_state? and labels_safe?,
  "deadline-timeout" => late_class == :timeout,
  "retry-decision-stop" => decision == :stop,
  "media-type-refused" =>
    reboot_class == :protocol and reboot_error.details.cause.code == :unexpected_response_media_type
}
```

## Public seam

`runtime.credentials` — `Wotex.Runtime.Credentials.resolve/4`
(consumer-implements; `StaticRef` resolves references at request time).
`http.client` — `Wotex.Binding.HTTP.Client` (`ReqClient`).

## Spec and completion IDs

* Lab: WLB.04 (`WLB-C04`, `WLB-C08`).
* Upstream consumer evidence: `RT-C02`, `RT-C03`, `WBH-C01`, `WBH-C03`.

## Replacement adapter

Implement `Wotex.Runtime.Credentials.resolve/4` against your secret store:
receive the selected security names and definitions, return `{:ok, %{name =>
credential}}` for that one call and never keep the secret in configuration.
For HTTP the credential is `{:bearer, token}` or `{:basic, user, password}`;
a scheme you do not support must be an error, not `nil`.
